00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.310
Are you stupid?

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:29.410
Takagi...

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:32.650
You always run off to the same spot whenever you have a problem.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:34.120
It's like you're a little kid.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.170
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.660
<i>Until then, everything had been normal.</i>

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.930
It's only the beginning of the semester.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:38.880
<i>There I was out in the sunshine</i>

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:44.330
<i>having a great time telling myself that out of all of the 2nd year students in the world,</i>

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.090
<i>I was the 4th most miserable one.</i>

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.610
<i>But at that time, everything...</i>

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.460
<i>...was more or less over.</i>

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.910
Whoa, Tejima-sensei!

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.420
Don't resort to violence...

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.330
<i>Looking back on it,</i>

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:32.210
<i>we should've just made our way outside.</i>

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:36.380
<i>Instead, we scrambled to the observatory.</i>

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.260
<i>Back then, it seemed like the best thing to do.</i>

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:41.400
Re--

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.200
Rei!

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:49.690
Why...

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.060
Why is this happening?

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:54.470
There must be a reason.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.320
If we knew the reason, we could figure out what to do.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:14.070
<i>Hisashi is always right.</i>

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:16.380
<i>I wanted to believe that too.</i>

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:25.590
<i>But I had this gut feeling that our world had already fallen apart.</i>

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:28.640
<i>So...</i>

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:30.350
<i>I...</i>

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.330
Gotcha!

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.730
Eat this!

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:46.900
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.540
<i>During that time,</i>

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.780
<i>it was too risky for us to think
that the world was still normal.</i>

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.210
Go away!

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.050
<i>Then it hit me.</i>

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:59.490
<i>We were walking through our school hallway carrying weapons and expecting to face danger.</i>

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:00.850
<i>It wasn't a hallway anymore.</i>

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.430
I'm sick of these things! I want my mom!

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.520
<i>Yeah... This is...</i>

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.360
<i>...the country of the dead.</i>

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.490
Do you think someone will come and help us?

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:20.090
No.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:21.800
But why?

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.400
How can you say that?

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.030
Remember the helicopters we saw from the school rooftop this afternoon? It's the same deal.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.590
No one can be bothered to help us.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:32.700
In fact, we might never...

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:33.740
Never?

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.660
We might never get any help?

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.250
Then how are we going to make it through this?!

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:42.260
We just have to do what we can. That's just the situation we're in.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.660
You're always like this...

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.700
You always say the wrong thing at the wrong time.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.640
You've been like this since kindergarten—

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.390
I was just stating the truth!

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:56.630
So?! You could say it different—

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:05.080
We should go.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:06.140
Yeah...

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:19.420
Should we act only in our own
self-interest, we stand not a chance.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.360
Let us act as a team.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:28.070
Let's go!

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:33.440
<i>Our actions at the time meant</i>

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:40.460
<i>that we were ready to take on the real problem and fight these animated pieces of flesh.</i>

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:48.260
<i>We ran through our school that was filled with noises, screams, life and death.</i>

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:51.530
They're not humans.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.400
They're not humans anymore!

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:18.250
It's dangerous outside!

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.960
Don't get out of your car under any circumstances!

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.460
I repeat!

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.980
Don't get out of your car under any circumstances!

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.740
We progress at roughly one kilometer an hour.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.790
I wonder if we can even make it over the bridge before morning at this rate?

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.690
Oh shut up! Put a lid on it!

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:44.080
Put a lid on it? But... I'm hungry...

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:53.930
There there.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.230
We're safe in here.

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:58.950
We'll be okay.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:00.860
Sensei...

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:03.490
There's nothing to worry about.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:07.420
We'll be o~kay.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:14.580
Well that's that.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:18.810
I've become the leader based on a majority vote.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:26.150
Rei!

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:28.610
Screw it!

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:31.570
No way in hell am I going to be anywhere near him!

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.050
Wait!

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.650
You just have to put up with him until we get to the city.

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:39.180
Didn't I tell you that you'd regret this?!

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:40.970
Look, now's not...

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:44.690
Dr. Marikawa!

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:51.380
<i>In other words, I didn't know yet</i>

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:55.430
<i>that this world had already ended.</i>

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.290
Komuro-kun! Are the two of you unharmed?

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:11.800
The police station!

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.160
We'll meet at the East Police Station.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.370
At what time?

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.300
7 PM!

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:22.000
If it doesn't work out today,
then we'll try again tomorrow!

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:52.250
There's... no one here.

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.490
Either they ran away, or they died.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.090
If they died, <i>they</i>'d be walking around!{Italics added -A0}

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:02.180
Then <i>they</i> went to chase after... living people...{Italics added -A0}

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:10.760
Look, Takashi!

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.070
License? Nope. Helmets? Nope. Bike? Stolen.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.650
He's gonna arrest us.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:24.390
Don't tell me you're afraid of a police car after beating up so many of <i>them</i>.{italics added (or did he beat up police cars? lol) -A0}

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:25.520
Of course I'm not.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:36.990
Are you serious?

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:39.800
Rei!

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:42.270
There's gas leaking from the car.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:43.220
Don't get close!

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.080
We might find something useful.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.340
What are you staring at?

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:50.810
You should help too!

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.450
Do you know how to use a gun?

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.930
I've seen some cop shows.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:16.500
You only put your finger on the trigger when you want to shoot, right?

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:25.830
Is something wrong?

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:29.120
It... feels kinda heavy.

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:31.910
Well duh. It's not a toy.

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:41.270
I only have five shots?

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:42.870
Here, Takashi.

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:51.420
It's from the other officer.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.160
His gun wasn't in working condition,

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:56.340
but you can still use the bullets.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:58.690
Wow, I'm amazed.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:02.350
I've seen the one my dad uses.

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:07.110
And do you think I'd be afraid of blood after what we've gone through?

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:18.390
Wanna throw these away?

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:21.230
Guns aren't exactly reliable if you don't know how to aim.

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:25.210
But you feel a bit safer now, don't you?

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:45.170
Self-Serve

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:45.170
Self-Serve

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.240
I wonder if they still have some gas.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:53.630
Every gas station has at least enough gas to fill up 1,000 cars.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:54.540
I'm sure they do.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:13:59.100
Shit.

00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:01.710
What is it?

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:04.260
This is a self-serve station.

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:06.710
We need to slide a card or put in some cash.

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:08.460
Then do it.

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:13.060
I bought a juice earlier... I only have 30 yen left.

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:15.940
You suck.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.690
Well excuse me for not being Hisashi!

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:23.600
What the hell's your problem?

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:26.030
When did I ever compare you with Hisashi?

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:27.660
You told me that I suck.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:30.150
That would mean there's someone awesome to compare me against!

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:32.010
You're obviously thinking of Hisashi!

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:36.680
You suck so much.

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:41.170
What do you want?

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:43.800
Cash! Can I borrow some?

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:48.210
Well, my purse is back in my bag.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.590
What, and you just told me that I suck?

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:55.900
Wait right here.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:57.530
Just scream if something happens.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:14.850
Is... anyone here?

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:28.040
Like that would open it...

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:32.200
Well, I've always wanted to try this.

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:40.770
What was that?

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:46.690
Wow, sounds like someone's having fun...

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:58.270
I should probably quit giving him a hard time...

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:09.350
Rei?

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.860
Hey! Stop moving!

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:17.150
Rei, what's wrong?

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:29.370
Hey bro! Your girl is pretty cute!

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:30.550
Let her go!

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:33.490
You dumb? Like hell I'd do that.

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:39.220
If I want to survive in this monster filled world, I need a woman.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:45.410
Are you... insane?

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.200
Am I insane?

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:48.900
Damn right I am!

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:53.160
My family all turned into those things right in front of me!

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:54.000
I...

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:58.580
I had to smash every single one of their heads!

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:02.840
My father, my mother, my grandmother, my little brother...

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:05.190
Even my sister, who's still in grade school!

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:08.310
How the fuck could I stay sane?

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:12.430
Takashi!

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:17.260
Rei!

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:21.410
Her tits and her voice are mighty fine!

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:25.420
And these are p-pretty big.

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:27.190
Hey...

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.160
You fuck her, right?

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.420
Every night, don't you?

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:34.640
Or... wait...

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.270
You don't?

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:38.760
Are you an idiot?!

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:45.870
Takashi!

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:48.490
Hey, toss me that bat!

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:51.390
If you don't, she's dead.

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:52.700
And...

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.400
I'm taking your bike.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:56.990
It's out of gas.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.980
You busted the cash register!

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:01.090
You've got tons of money!

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.770
Refill the damn thing!

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:25.520
<i>Please place your hand on the 
static discharge button before you begin.{"a
resistive seat" to "the 
static discharge button" for flow -A0}</i>

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:28.720
Hey...

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:30.600
Can you let us go?

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:35.960
We're on our way to see if our parents are safe.

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:39.390
Weren't you listening to a thing I said?!

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:43.830
If they're in town, then your
parents met the same fate as mine!

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:46.030
Done.

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:49.260
Then go!

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:50.590
Just go!

00:18:58.050 --> 00:18:59.630
Hey, can you—

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:01.770
Shut up! Do you want me to kill you too?!

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.780
Hey, please—

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:11.040
Shut up!

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:13.780
Or I'll seriously fucking kill you!

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.700
I've never fired a gun before,

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:28.960
but I can't miss at point-blank range.

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:32.590
Wh-What if it ignites the gasoline?

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:36.130
It's a lot better than giving you my girl.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:53.300
FUCK!

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.960
Bl-Blood... BLOOD!

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:02.850
How... dare you...

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.050
Don't do it, Rei.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:06.430
But!

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:09.460
We don't have time to deal with him.

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:11.000
After all...

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:14.020
That noise we made was loud.

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:23.240
Hey!

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.790
You're just gonna leave?

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.530
You're gonna leave me here?

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:28.640
Come on! Help me!

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:30.360
Please, help me!

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:33.810
Hey!

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.640
Hey...

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:07.560
「Aa yami ga owaru」 to

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:07.560
Once the sorrow dissipates,

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:07.560
「ああ、闇が終わる」と

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:14.100
Kuroku yodomu kimi no me ga tsubuyaku

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:14.100
buds sprout out of the darkness and begin to grow

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:14.100
黒く淀む君の目が呟く

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:18.170
Tada Kuzureta Sekai

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:18.170
I'm in a world that has fallen to ruins

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:18.170
ただ崩れた世界

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:26.530
Ashita e no ikiba sura nakushite Dakedo

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:26.530
I had lost my way toward tomorrow,

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:26.530
明日への行き場すら無くして だけど

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:31.930
Mamorubeki Hito Koe ga Michibiku

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:31.930
but the voice of the one I must protect guides me

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:31.930
守るべき人声が導く

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:38.830
Namida o Mou Minai to Kimeta Toki

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:38.830
When I swore to never see her cry again,

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:38.830
涙をもう見ないと決めた時

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:42.970
Kokoro no Kase Kowashite

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:42.970
I freed my heart of its shackles

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:42.970
心の枷壊して

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:47.880
Ima Todaeru Kodou o

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:47.880
and grasped a burning blade

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:47.880
今　凍える心　

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:55.000
honoo de tokasu ha wo nigirishime

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:55.000
A blade that would melt my heart into fire

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:55.000
炎で溶かす　刃を握り締め

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:59.890
Ima Fureru Yubi o

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:59.890
As my fingers tremble,

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:59.890
今　震える指を　

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:06.600
Hikigane no Kuro ni Tsuyoku Ategau

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:06.600
I firmly place them on my heavy, black trigger

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:06.600
引き金の黒に　強く宛てがう

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:19.420
Kono Inochi o Tada  Kuuki no Tama ni Kaete

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:19.420
and turn my life into a shot of air

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:19.420
この命をただ狂気の弾に変えて

00:22:33.550 --> 00:22:34.790
Is something wrong, Takashi?

00:22:35.430 --> 00:22:36.130
You haven't said anything.

00:22:38.420 --> 00:22:42.070
As we keep moving, we'll probably see that same thing happen over and over.

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:44.110
Really?

00:22:45.290 --> 00:22:47.350
Yeah... You're right.

00:22:50.360 --> 00:22:51.850
Forget about it.

00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:52.650
Let's hurry.

00:22:57.440 --> 00:22:59.340
<i>Of course, I never forgot about it.</i>

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:03.120
<i>The first day after the world came to an end,</i>

00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:07.160
<i>I was responsible for someone's death.</i>

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:11.530
<i>I couldn't possibly forget that.</i>

00:23:26.440 --> 00:23:27.400
Crazy.

00:23:27.540 --> 00:23:29.600
This is worse than a war...

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:33.880
Boom!

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:35.410
What a fine man you are, Hirano-kun.{"You are a man, Hirano-kun." to "What a fine man you are, Hirano-kun." to match Ep.5 -A0}
